analysisWe need to produce an assert statement reflecting the comment.

The comment: "// @@@ If the element is not null, then it is contained in the priority queue after the operation."

Method: public boolean offer(E e)

We need to assert that if e != null then after the operation (i.e., after method returns) the queue contains e. Use this.contains(e). Since contains is observer method defined earlier. Also need to include premise about e not null. So assert e != null => this.contains(e);

But also note that the method throws NullPointerException if e is null, so after operation e is guaranteed not null (since method would have thrown). However the spec says "If the element is not null, then it is contained". So we can write:

assert e != null => this.contains(e);

